      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "| $x$ | $-4.5$ | $-3.5$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1.5$ | $2$ | $4.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $3$ | $0$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\nThe root of the function $f(x)$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given table, we see that $f(-2)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x=-2.$",
