      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190079/assets/acc14b61036a00f4fae8d850954293c99d48388a8b4a83dda158bf1688d97c62.png)\n\nWhat are the roots of the function $f(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?\n\nIn **ascending order**, the roots are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that $f(3)=0$ and $f(4)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=3$ and $x=4.$",
