    "q-60890": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60890",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "What is the root of the function $f(x)=3x-6?$",
      "worked_solution": "The roots are the solutions to the equation $f(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ 3x-6 & =0 \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=2.$",
